    "lastText": "`ledger` is built and does everything TASK.md describes. All 10 acceptance criteria pass, `npm test` runs 50 tests with none skipped, and the final audit returned PASS.\n\n- **CLI:** every command works through `node bin/ledger.js` — `add` (with `--repeat monthly --times`), `list`, `balance`, `delete`, `edit`, `budget set`/`budget status`, `import`, `export`, `report`, `undo`, and `--help`/`help`. `--file` works anywhere after the command name. Errors go to stderr with exit code 2.\n- **Library:** `Ledger` in `src/ledger.js` has `add`, `list`, `balance`, `remove` and `update`, and saves to the file on every change.\n- **Data handling:** amounts are stored as integer cents, so 0.1 + 0.2 prints `0.30`. Writes are atomic, and ids are never reused.\n- **Docs:** `README.md` documents every command with an example.\n\nOne decision beyond the spec: undo history is stored in the ledger file itself, so `undo` works across separate runs.\n\nUndoing an `add` does not roll the id counter back, so the next `add` after an undo gets a fresh id rather than reusing the undone one.",
